# EAGLES — Antigravity UI/UX Design System Rules

These rules govern all presentation layer, styling, and client UI/UX engineering in EAGLES.
Full charter: [`ANTIGRAVITY.md`](../../ANTIGRAVITY.md).
Audit & Measurements: [`docs/05_UI/04_Modernization_Audit.md`](../../docs/05_UI/04_Modernization_Audit.md).

---

## 1. The Presentation-Only Firewall (Strict Rule)

You are acting on the **presentation layer only**.
* **NEVER** edit or create files in `prisma/`, `src/features/*/services/`, or `src/features/*/repositories/`.
* **NEVER** modify route handler contracts (`src/app/api/`), DTO models, or server-side authorization checks (`src/features/authorization/`).
* **NEVER** alter ranking math (`fractional-indexing`), OCC versioning (`version: Int`), or data calculations.
* All data fetching in client components must go through existing typed hooks or `apiRequest` (`src/shared/lib/api-client.ts`).

---

## 2. Layout & Viewport Rules

* **Full-Bleed by Default:** The workspace region must fill `100%` of available width (`calc(100vw - sidebarWidth)`).
* **Ban on Unbounded Margins:** Never use `max-w-*` with `mx-auto` on page bodies. All page wrappers must use `<AppFrame>`. Dead gutters on 1080p+ displays are considered a defect.
* **Sticky Chrome, Scrolling Workspace:** The top bar (48px) and toolbar (40px) stay fixed. The workspace area (`flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-auto`) scrolls internally.
* **Collapse Vertical Height:** Total chrome above a board or table must not exceed ~130px.

---

## 3. Surface & Elevation Rules (Eradicating Card Nesting)

* **No Card-in-Card Nesting:** Never place a bordered, rounded card inside another card or panel. Lists, rows, and items inside a panel must be borderless rows separated by subtle 1px divider lines (`border-b border-border/50`).
* **Material 3 Tonal Surfaces:** Panels sit on `--canvas`. Modals, popovers, and drawers use `--surface-raised`. Toolbars and table headers use `--surface-sunken`.
* **Subtle Hairline Elevation:** Depth comes from 1px crisp borders (`#E0E2EC` / `border-border`) paired with subtle ambient contact shadows, not heavy dark drop-shadows.

---

## 4. Design Token Scales (No Arbitrary Utilities)

* **Radius Scale (3 steps only):**
  * `--radius-sm` (`4px`): Badges, status chips, checkboxes, tags.
  * `--radius-md` (`6px`): Buttons, inputs, dropdown items, tabs.
  * `--radius-lg` (`8px`): Panels, cards, dialogs, drawers.
  * *Banned:* `rounded-xl`, `rounded-2xl`, `rounded-3xl` on containers. `rounded-full` is reserved for avatars and circular icon buttons.
* **Spacing Scale (4px base):**
  * `4px` (`--space-1`), `8px` (`--space-2`), `12px` (`--space-3`), `16px` (`--space-4`), `20px` (`--space-5`), `24px` (`--space-6`), `32px` (`--space-8`).
* **Typography Roles (Accessible Floor = 11px):**
  * `page-title` (20px / 600)
  * `section-title` (15px / 600)
  * `body` (13px / 400) & `body-strong` (13px / 500)
  * `label` (12px / 500)
  * `meta` (11px / 400)
  * *Banned:* Text sizes below 11px (9px and 10px are forbidden).

---

## 5. Density & Component Standards

* **Density Default:** Data surfaces (tables, boards, backlogs, logs) default to **Compact**:
  * Table rows: 32px height (40px in Comfortable mode).
  * Inputs and buttons: 28px height in compact toolbars, 32px standard.
  * Panel internal padding: 12px compact / 16px comfortable.
* **Tables:** Always use the shared `<DataTable>` component built on `@tanstack/react-table`. Never write hand-rolled `<table>` or ad-hoc flexbox rows for data collections.
* **Inspect Drawers:** When a user clicks an item for details, slide out `<Drawer>` from the right edge rather than navigating away or launching an intrusive dialog.
